    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0174" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/6–2047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in India
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-20T17:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1947—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. June 19 Reuter despatch reports selection Karachi as capital Pakistan and
                    quotes Minnigerode<anchor n="1" xml:id="d98-f1"/> as stating that “question of
                    establishing an American Embassy here was engaging the attention of US
                    authorities”.</p>
                <pb facs="0175" n="157" xml:id="pg157"/>
                <p>Dept appreciates fact Minnigerode may have been misquoted<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d98-f2"/> but wishes stress need avoid premature indication any US
                    intentions re establishment additional dip missions in India or that question is
                    engaging question [<hi rendition="#italic">attention?</hi>] US authorities this
                    time.</p>
                <p>Sent New Delhi, repeated Karachi and London. Delhi to inform other
                    consulates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d98-f1" n="1" xml:id="d98-f1-content">
                <p>Holdsworth G. Minnigerode, Consul at Karachi.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d98-f2" n="2" xml:id="d98-f2-content">
                <p>Minnigerode informed the Department, in telegram 39, June 23, from Karachi, that
                    the Reuters dispatch allegedly quoting him was “utterly false,” and that he had
                    limited his June 17 remarks before a delegation of eight newspapermen to the
                    comment that he had no information on the subject of establishing an American
                    Embassy at Karachi and was unable and unauthorized to make any statement
                    (845.00/6–2347).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
